  "question": "1) Background / Context\nThe project involves developing a powerful Content Management System (CMS) using Ruby on Rails 5.2+. This CMS, known as \"Comfortable Mexican Sofa,\" integrates seamlessly into existing Rails applications with minimal configuration and remains isolated from other application components.\n\n 2) Objectives\nThe primary goal is to provide a robust, flexible CMS solution that supports multiple sites and languages, including features like page templating, revision history, and an extendable admin area, enhancing both user and administrative experiences.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Developers: Interested in easy integration and customization capabilities.\n- Content Managers: Require multi-language support and tools for content manipulation.\n- Administrators: Need efficient site management, content revision, and localization support.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n- Integration: Simple drop-in integration with Ruby on Rails 5.2+ applications.\n- Page Templating: Utilize Content Tags for flexible page layout creation.\n- Multi-Site Support: Manage multiple websites from a single installation.\n- Multi-Language Support: Offers internationalization (i18n) covering languages such as English, Spanish, German, French, Chinese, and more.\n- Initial Content Population (CMS Seeds): Enable quick setup with predefined content.\n- Revision History: Track changes and allow reversion to previous states.\n- Admin Area: Extensible interface designed with Bootstrap 4, featuring responsive design.\n- Editing Tools: Use CodeMirror for HTML and Markdown syntax highlighting and Redactor as the WYSIWYG editor.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Scalability: The CMS should efficiently manage multiple sites and large content repositories.\n- Usability: The admin interface must be user-friendly and extensible.\n- Localization: Comprehensive multi-language support and page localization are essential.\n- Performance: The system must ensure prompt rendering of content and handle high traffic efficiently.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0008\nCREATE TABLE `sites` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `hostname` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `locale` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `index_sites_on_hostname` (`hostname`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `layouts` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `site_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `identifier` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `label` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `index_layouts_on_site_id_and_identifier` (`site_id`,`identifier`),\n  KEY `index_layouts_on_site_id` (`site_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `layouts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`site_id`) REFERENCES `sites` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `pages` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `site_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `parent_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `layout_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `slug` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `content` longtext DEFAULT NULL,\n  `published` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `position` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `index_pages_on_site_id_and_path` (`site_id`,`path`),\n  KEY `index_pages_on_site_id` (`site_id`),\n  KEY `index_pages_on_parent_id` (`parent_id`),\n  KEY `index_pages_on_layout_id` (`layout_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `pages_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`site_id`) REFERENCES `sites` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `pages_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`parent_id`) REFERENCES `pages` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `pages_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`layout_id`) REFERENCES `layouts` (`id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `page_translations` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `page_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `locale` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `content` longtext DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `index_page_translations_on_page_id_and_locale` (`page_id`,`locale`),\n  KEY `index_page_translations_on_page_id` (`page_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `page_translations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`page_id`) REFERENCES `pages` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `revisions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `revisable_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `revisable_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `site_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `locale` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `content` longtext NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `index_revisions_on_revisable_type_and_revisable_id` (`revisable_type`,`revisable_id`),\n  KEY `index_revisions_on_site_id` (`site_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `revisions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`site_id`) REFERENCES `sites` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
